  "body": "## What changed\n- `crates/app/tests/default_machine_missing/disk_recovery.rs`: the parent test makes the folder with `join(\"assets\").join(\"machines\")`. Before, it used `join(\"assets/machines\")`.\n- `check_disk_recovery` builds the compared path the same way.\n- The reader does not change.\n- `docs/decisions/4120-windows-path-sep.md` records the decision.\n\n## Cause\nOn Windows, `join(\"assets/machines\")` keeps the `/`. The path becomes `...\\.tmpXXXX\\assets/machines`. The reader prints `...\\assets\\machines`. The `missing.contains(machines.to_str())` check then fails. On Linux and macOS the two strings are the same, so the test passes there.\n\n## Tests\n- Pin: `disk_recovery::a_repaired_default_machine_file_is_read_again_through_the_disk_reader`.\n- macOS: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test default_machine_missing`: 10 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 1 step, `app default_machine_missing (disk_recovery::)`, ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Red before the fix: not shown. The failure occurs only on Windows. I did not run on Windows. On macOS the old and the new code both pass.\n- Mutation check: not possible on macOS, for the same reason. The test still compares the reader message with the isolated folder path. Thus a reader that does not use the isolated folder still fails the test.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone. This is a test-only change. No post, toolpath or recorded program changes, so the example catalog and heavy lanes are not reached.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Windows. I did not run this test on Windows. The M5 session runs the Windows check (`bacon`, `lenny` or `winnie`) after this PR opens.\n\n## Overlaps\nNone. No open PR changes this file.\n\nEffort: low\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #4120\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
